With a fingerprint persona (--fingerprint, unless --disable-spoofing contains
"font"), web content on macOS only sees the fonts that ship with the system in
/System/Library/Fonts. Fonts macOS downloaded for the host's languages
(/System/Library/AssetsV2) or that were installed separately behave as if they
were not installed: font-family and local() lookups do not find them, and
per-character fallback takes the first system font of the --lang cascade list
that can draw the character instead. Without --fingerprint, behaviour is
unchanged.

